{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# SuperBase process flow\nJon's five steps (Capability Statement pp.3–4) with the key frames that show each one.\n\n[[Process Overview]] · [[Footage Index]] · [[00 Home]]","x":0,"y":-640,"width":780,"height":160},
		{"id":"cbr","type":"text","text":"## The proof loop (CBR)\n1. **Yard walk**, then nominate one **trial area**\n2. **Soaked CBR before treatment**, lab-tested on your own yard material\n3. **Treat**: steps 01 to 05 below, dosed for that material\n4. **Density** confirmed on site against the dosage design (step 04)\n5. **Soaked CBR after cure**, then the **trial report** (CBR before and after, depth and density, dosage rate)\n6. **Roll out by area**, then hand over to your crew\n\n*None of this loop is in the footage yet. Never put a CBR number on screen.*","x":420,"y":-420,"width":1260,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"s1","type":"text","text":"## 01 Prepare\nGrade off loose stone and bull dust; scarify the existing base to ~75 mm; import roadbase only where levels need it.\n\n**Footage ◐** [[V01 - Prepare|V01]] 0.0–10.0 s: track loader on the loose base (Jon's p.3 photo = 2.5–3.0 s). Scarifying itself not shown.\n\n[[Step 1 - Prepare]]","x":0,"y":0,"width":360,"height":220},
		{"id":"s2","type":"text","text":"## 02 Dose and mix\nSuperBase in with water at a ratio set for your base, mixed through the full depth.\n\n**Footage ◐** [[V02A - Dose and Mix A|V02A]]: water cart \"740\" and hand hose (dose only). No mixing through depth; liquid not confirmed as SuperBase.\n\n[[Step 2 - Dose and Mix]]","x":420,"y":0,"width":360,"height":220},
		{"id":"s3","type":"text","text":"## 03 Grade to level\nTrim the treated base to design level and crossfall while it's workable, so water can't pond.\n\n**Footage: none.** No grader in any clip. Jon's p.3 photo for this step is a roller still (V03C / V04 ≈0.77 s).\n\n[[Step 3 - Grade to Level]]","x":840,"y":0,"width":360,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"s4","type":"text","text":"## 04 Roll and compact\nWet rolling to final compaction with a smooth-drum roller; density checked against the dosage design.\n\n**Footage ✅** [[V02B - Dose and Mix B|V02B]] (wet), [[V03A - Roll and Compact A|V03A]], [[V03B - Roll and Compact B|V03B]], [[V03C - Roll and Compact C|V03C]] (= V04). 65.3 s unique.\n\n[[Step 4 - Roll and Compact]]","x":1260,"y":0,"width":360,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s5","type":"text","text":"## 05 Cure and return to service\nCures to a bound hardstand, trafficable within hours of the final roll; organic top coat on running lines.\n\n**Footage ◐ stills only.** [[S04 - Cure Stills|S04B]] cured canopy pad; S04A trafficked yard (other site). V04 is rolling, not cure.\n\n[[Step 5 - Cure and Return to Service]]","x":1680,"y":0,"width":360,"height":220},
